  "source": {
    "hand_crafted": true,
    "expected_from": "reasoned",
    "rationale": "§10 follow-up (3b). The LLM sometimes emits the LITERAL STRING 'null' for a hint. That is truthy, so left alone it mis-fires the domain->business_query clobber, deriveRouting and the blocklist. norm() must coerce 'null' (and '') to real null. Item 0 sends 'null' for both hints and item 1 sends '' - both must come out as real null, and because domain_hint is then falsy deriveRouting is never called and routing falls through to the PRIOR turn's warehouse team. Item 2 is the control: a REAL domain string passes through norm untouched, so deriveRouting runs and routes the turn to customer_service/order_enquiries instead. The prior team is deliberately a different one from item 2's derived team, or the coercion would be invisible in routing.",
    "amended": [
      {
